  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "He Xiangjian (Chinese: 何享健; pinyin: Hé Xiǎngjiàn; Jyutping: Ho4 Hoeng2 Gin6, born 5 October 1942) is the co-founder of Midea, one of China's largest appliance makers. In September 2021, his net worth was estimated to be $28.8 billion by Bloomberg Billionaires Index, positioning him at the 51st place in the index.\n\n",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
